<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51449" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vultŭrĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">volt-</span></b> ), ii, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				vulture</i>, <i>bird of prey.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Truc. 2, 3, 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Most.
				3, 2, 146</span></i> sqq.; <i><span class="en">Lucr. 4, 680</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 27,
				23, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">27, 11,
				4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">41, 21,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A vulture;</i> a designation for <i>a
				rapacious</i> or <i>covetous person</i>, <i>an extortioner</i>, and the like: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sunt alii qui te volturium vocant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Trin. 1, 2, 64</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vulturius illius provinciae imperator,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Pis. 16, 38</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cat. 68, 124</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>An unlucky throw</i> at dice: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jacit vulturios quattuor. Talos arripio: jacto
					basilicum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Curc. 2, 3, 78</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
